# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Course materials

# Session material never enters the repo. files/sessionNN/ is a local staging
# folder; the zip built from it is copied to ~/Dropbox/mgmt638-files/ and the
# schedule links the Dropbox share URL. A session zip is tens of megabytes --
# committing one puts it in the history permanently, and replacing it later
# adds the whole size again rather than swapping it.
#
# Ignoring the staged contents also keeps them off the site: Quarto treats
# every non-ignored project file as a resource and mirrors it into docs/.
# .gitkeep stays tracked so the empty folders survive a clone.
*.zip
# Session 7 is the exception, by decision: its zip is published from the repo
# rather than Dropbox, so the Files link on the schedule is self-hosted. Both
# copies have to be un-ignored -- the staged one and the one Quarto copies into
# docs/ from the resources: list. It is 19.7MB and it is in history for good;
# re-zipping later adds the whole size again rather than replacing it.
!files/session07.zip
!docs/files/session07.zip
# Session 8 follows the same exception: the reading and the lecture video for
# Sep 17 ship as a repo-hosted zip rather than a Dropbox link. 21.9MB, also
# permanent in history.
!files/session08.zip
!docs/files/session08.zip
# Session 9 likewise: the JBSS, FLXS, and SMID data folders for the Sep 22
# group exercise (sept22.html links files/session09.zip). 3.9MB.
!files/session09.zip
!docs/files/session09.zip
files/session*/*
!files/session*/.gitkeep
QuantEquity/

